# Keep line endings the same everywhere.
#
# The shell scripts run on the intercom, which is Linux. A file that picked up Windows line
# endings on the way through fails there with a message that names the wrong thing: the
# shell reads the carriage return as part of the command and says the command does not
# exist.
#
# So every text file is stored and checked out with Unix line endings, on all three
# systems. PowerShell does not mind them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
*.fwz binary
